      "nets": ["Net-(D5-A)", "NET0005", "Net-(D9-A)", "NET0001"],
      "observed": "Both fan-tach signal paths have series diodes oriented with their cathodes toward the fan headers and anodes toward the MCU-side pull-ups and inputs: D5.3 is on NET0005 with J9.3, while D5.1 is on Net-(D5-A) with R1 and GPIO21; D9.3 is on NET0001 with J1.3, while D9.1 is on Net-(D9-A) with R5 and GPIO20. The MCU-side pull-ups are 10 kΩ to +3V3.",
      "expected": "The tach inputs should pass fan tach pulses to the MCU. For the usual open-collector fan tach output, the low-going pulses must be able to pull the MCU input low; the series diode orientation should not block that path.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"D5\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"K\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"J9\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"Pin_3\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"D5\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"31\") (pinfunction \"GPIO21/U0TXD\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"D9\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"K\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"J1\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"Pin_3\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"D9\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"30\") (pinfunction \"GPIO20/U0RXD\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"R1\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"R5\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "Monitors 2 fan tachometers (NUM_FANS = 2) with TVS-diode-protected inputs, and raises a run fault if a fan stalls."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "With typical open-collector fan tach outputs, a low pulse at either header reverse-biases the series diode, so the MCU-side input remains pulled high instead of seeing the pulse. Fan speed/stall monitoring may therefore fail for both fans.",
      "confidence": 0.94
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The fan tach signal paths appear to have their series diodes reversed relative to the MCU-side pull-ups. This likely blocks the low-going pulses produced by standard open-collector fan tach outputs, undermining the specified fan monitoring."
}

